---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { PHONE, TEL_HREF, TOWNS } from '../data/site';
import { TOWN_PAGES } from '../data/towns';

// Towns with their own page link through. The rest stay as plain chips.
const townHref = new Map(TOWN_PAGES.map((t) => [t.name, `/european-auto-repair/${t.slug}`]));

const title = 'Service Area for Mobile European Auto Repair | Eway Auto Repairs';
const description = `Mobile European car repair across Camden, Burlington and Gloucester counties: Cherry Hill, Marlton, Moorestown, Voorhees, Medford, Mount Laurel and more. I come to you. Call ${PHONE}.`;
---

<Page title={title} description={description} path="/service-area">
  <PageIntro eyebrow="Service Area">
    <Fragment slot="title">
      South Jersey, <span class="accent">driveway to driveway</span>.
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="intro">
      Camden, Burlington, and Gloucester counties. Home or work, driveway or office lot.
      Diagnostics and most repairs happen wherever the car already is.
    </Fragment>
  </PageIntro>

  <section class="section-ruled">
    <div class="section container">
      <h2 data-reveal>Towns I cover</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">
        If your town isn't on the list, call and ask. This is where I am most often, not a
        hard boundary.
      </p>
      <div class="town-row">
        {
          TOWNS.map((t) =>
            townHref.has(t) ? (
              <a class="town-chip" href={townHref.get(t)} data-tile>
                {t}
              </a>
            ) : (
              <span class="town-chip" data-tile>
                {t}
              </span>
            )
          )
        }
      </div>

      <h2 style="margin-top:64px" data-reveal>Town by town</h2>
      <div class="rule" data-rule></div>
      <p class="section-intro" data-reveal>
        Each of these has its own quirks, from the dealership density in Cherry Hill to the
        long driveways out in Medford. Here is what the work usually looks like in each.
      </p>
      <div class="failure-list">
        {
          TOWN_PAGES.map((t) => (
            <a
              class="failure-item"
              href={`/european-auto-repair/${t.slug}`}
              data-reveal
              style="display:block"
            >
              <h3 style="color:var(--accent)">{t.name}, NJ</h3>
              <p>{t.intro}</p>
            </a>
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <div class="copy" style="margin-top:56px">
        <p>
          Mobile isn't a compromise for most of this work. Diagnostics, inspections,
          maintenance, brakes, and a good share of repairs don't need a lift. They need the
          right tools and somebody who knows the car. What you skip is the drop-off, the
          shuttle ride, and three days of arranging your life around a service department.
        </p>
        <p>
          There are jobs that belong in a shop with a lift, and when yours is one of them I'll
          say so and help you sort out the right way to handle it. Nothing gets started in a
          driveway that shouldn't be.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="next-links">
        <a class="chip-link" href="/services">What I do on site</a>
        <a class="chip-link" href="/pre-purchase-inspection">Inspections at the seller's location</a>
        <a class="chip-link" href="/contact">Check if I cover your town</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    title="Not sure if you're in range?"
    sub={`Call ${PHONE} with your town. If I can't get to you I'll say so right away.`}
  />
</Page>
